{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py | sed -n '18,255p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md | sed -n '1,170p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# \"Forecast unavailable\" for number questions: the design, ready for when release work opens\n     2\t\n     3\t**Status: design only. Nothing is built.** Alex decided the behaviour twice:\n     4\t- D726, \"同意\": until the number answers pass, a first release shows number questions with their sources and \"Forecast unavailable\",\n     5\t  with the band, the forecast text and its history withheld together; \"it is built with the release work, which is not started\";\n     6\t- D756, \"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线\".\n     7\t\n     8\tOpening release work is Alex's call (council 72). This page makes the build a known, reviewed slice for that moment.\n     9\t\n    10\t**Revision 4 (council 72c) of revision 3: one structural rule instead of a list of leaks.** Rounds 72 and 72b each found new paths by which a withheld forecast\n    11\tcould reach a reader:\n    12\t- the idea card;\n    13\t- the closing text;\n    14\t- an idea summary that re-reads the ladder;\n    15\t- a release page that reloads from the live POC service;\n    16\t- a translated export;\n    17\t- a Yes/No explanation that quotes a number question's band.\n    18\t\n    19\tA rule that withholds fields reader by reader will keep missing one (AGENTS §1: \"when one mechanism draws findings round after round,\n    20\tstop answering findings: propose one structural rule\"). Revision 3 replaces that rule with an allow-list at one boundary.\n    21\t\n    22\t## 1. The gap, measured at $0 (2026-11-23)\n    23\t\n    24\tThe stored poc-v118 store `poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/views.sqlite`, read-only, gives:\n    25\t- **The number question v8 (FY2027 Data Center revenue)** exposes its band, label, condition, reasons, 75 judgements and 69 change rows.\n    26\t- **Its idea input** reads \"Bullish … $350 billion to under $400 billion\".\n    27\t- **Yes/No explanations quote number forecasts:**\n    28\t  - `old-3` `v36`, judgement 799: \"around $1 trillion\" for 2027 spending;\n    29\t  - `old-1` `v10`, judgement 865: the selected bands of both spending questions.\n    30\t\n    31\t  The judge is shown related questions' selected bands (`views/judging.py:208`), and its prose can repeat them.\n    32\t\n    33\t## 2. The structural rule: one release export, allow-listed\n    34\t\n    35\t- **One exporter writes the release data:** `release_export`, a single function beside `service.py`. It emits only the fields on an\n    36\t  explicit allow-list. A field not on the list cannot appear, so a new or overlooked path fails closed.\n    37\t- **The release builder calls `release_export` directly** and accepts no external input; a marker or version names a format, not\n    38\t  who wrote the text (council 72c). The finished package is checked as well as the page: it holds only the export's output, with no\n    39\t  market data, composite trials or translated file beside it.\n    40\t- **The release reads only that export.** Its page, its static build and its API, if any, read nothing else:\n    41\t  - no live POC service;\n    42\t  - no `/library` reload (`poc/ui/src/bootstrap.js` must not fetch in a release build);\n    43\t  - no prepared or translated JSON (`scripts/mock_translate.py`'s `data.en.json`);\n    44\t  - no `--composite-trials` input.\n    45\t\n    46\t  The static builder refuses any input not produced by `release_export`, which carries a marker and the allow-list version.\n    47\t- **For a number question, the allow-list is:**\n    48\t  - the question and its id;\n    49\t  - the evidence in force: one-line, quote, speaker, original day, tier and sources, amounts as quoted;\n    50\t  - the marker \"Forecast unavailable\".\n    51\t\n    52\t  Nothing else is listed:\n    53\t  - no ladder;\n    54\t  - no band, label or condition;\n    55\t  - no reasons or why_changed;\n    56\t  - no history, counts or assessment dates;\n    57\t  - no closing band (\"closed\" only);\n    58\t  - no theme pushes, no composite, no idea derived from its forecast.\n    59\t- **Ideas.** The release's idea composition (`idea.py`, `idea_composite.py`) runs on export data only. A number question enters it\n    60\t  as question and evidence with the marker. Its ladder is not read from storage in either the answer-format build or the summary\n    61\t  input (`idea_composite.py:255`, `:281`; `poc-v118-idea.json:94`). The test inspects the composed request itself, not only the\n    62\t  delivered card.\n    63\t- **The POC is unchanged.** Its API, MCP and page keep today's behaviour. Whether colleagues' POC page also changes is a separate\n    64\t  later choice for Alex.\n    65\t\n    66\t## 3. Identity: what a number question is (verified on four stores by council 72b)\n    67\t\n    68\tA view is a number question unless one of the following excludes it:\n    69\t1. **An event.** The view key's measure is in `identity.EVENT_MEASURES` (`event`, `policy_event`). That covers 85 of 85 event\n    70\t   questions in the three comparison stores.\n    71\t2. **A Yes/No question.** The ladder has exactly two labels which, canonicalised with the existing vocabulary\n    72\t   (`vocabulary.canonical`), are Yes and No in either order. The sealed ledger's 30 such questions use `是` and `否`. The Xbox `v37`\n    73\t   (`growth_rate`, bounds around zero) is Yes/No.\n    74\t\n    75\tEvery other view is a number question. Its forecast is withheld whether its bands come from `lo`/`hi`, parse from the conditions\n    76\t(the sealed `v3`), or cannot be resolved. An unresolved record is withheld and listed in the release check, with a key or without\n    77\t(council 72b: an `old-1/v8` copy without bounds does not parse, and its key still exists).\n    78\t\n    79\tCounts (council 72b), number / event or Yes/No:\n    80\t- `old-1` 19 / 28, `old-2` 17 / 26, `old-3` 18 / 31;\n    81\t- the sealed ledger: 43 parse as money, 21 are withheld as unresolved, 30 are Yes/No.\n    82\t\n    83\tNo wrong show-or-withhold result was found.\n    84\t\n    85\t**Events are binary too.** All 85 comparison-store events are also two-answer questions, including both known prose leaks, and a\n    86\tbinary event such as \"Restriction adopted\" / \"No restriction adopted\" exists in the served ledger (council 72c). §4's rule applies to\n    87\tevery question that is not a number question, events and Yes/No alike, and each keeps its answer label.\n    88\t\n    89\t## 4. Questions that are not number questions: an open choice for Alex (not decided here)\n    90\t\n    91\tD726 covers number questions. A Yes/No question's band is not a number forecast, but its stored explanation can quote one (§1). The\n    92\tallow-list must say which Yes/No fields the release shows:\n    93\t- **(a)** the question, its evidence and its answer (Yes/No and label), with no explanation text. Safe, and it removes the reasoning\n    94\t  readers would see.\n    95\t- **(b)** as (a), plus the explanation only for judgements whose request showed the judge no number question's state. Code can\n    96\t  decide this from the stored request (`views/judging.py`, which builds the related questions shown).\n    97\t- **Measured (council 72c),** matching each judgement to its archived request:\n    98\t  - (b) would keep explanations on 31 of 769, 44 of 776 and 43 of 958 judgements in the three comparison runs;\n    99\t  - for a reader at the latest answer, it would keep them on 21 of 85 questions;\n   100\t  - it would keep 73 of 73 in the sealed ledger.\n   101\t- **The limit of (b).** It cannot promise the prose quotes no number forecast. A request also carries the question's own previous\n   102\t  reasoning, and can carry another question's, either of which may repeat a forecast seen earlier. Both known leaks are in\n   103\t  `why_changed`.\n   104\t- **Recommendation: (a) for the first release** (council 72c; Claude agrees, withdrawing its lean for (b)). It is the only option\n   105\t  that guarantees no number forecast reaches a reader through prose. (b) remains a measured later step.\n   106\t\n   107\t## 5. Tests and the $0 release check (each names its row above)\n   108\t\n   109\t- **Fixtures (real store on a temporary path):**\n   110\t  - a number question with `lo`/`hi`;\n   111\t  - one with bounds only in its conditions;\n   112\t  - an unresolved one with a key;\n   113\t  - a Yes/No question with numeric bounds;\n   114\t  - an event question;\n   115\t  - a Yes/No judgement whose prose quotes a number band;\n   116\t  - a real closing switch;\n   117\t  - an idea.\n   118\t- **What the tests assert.** `release_export`'s output holds only allow-listed keys (a schema check that fails on any extra key). For\n   119\t  number questions it holds no band, ladder, reasons, history, date or closing band; Yes/No follows §4's choice. The static build\n   120\t  refuses foreign input, and a release page makes no network fetch.\n   121\t- **Mutants:**\n   122\t  - an extra field;\n   123\t  - a fetch left on;\n   124\t  - a ladder read in idea composition;\n   125\t  - the identity mis-sorting each fixture.\n   126\t\n   127\t  Each must fail.\n   128\t- **End-to-end acceptance (council 72c):**\n   129\t  - an idea whose only question is `old-1/v8`: the card keeps its sources and \"Forecast unavailable\", with no scored driver and no\n   130\t    substitute band (the current composite expects an endpoint for every scoring candidate, `idea_composite.py:214`, `:231`);\n   131\t  - in the same release package, the two known event answers keep their labels and carry no spending forecast under the chosen\n   132\t    prose rule.\n   133\t- **The $0 release check.**\n   134\t  - On `old-1/v8`, confirm the marker and the same sources in the page and in the export data.\n   135\t  - Exercise closure on a temporary copy with a real closing switch, after first confirming that the unrestricted response exposes the\n   136\t    final band there.\n   137\t  - Check ideas with a recorded or test transport, inspecting the composed request.\n   138\t  - Use `old-3/v36` and `old-1/v10` as the Yes/No prose cases.\n   139\t  - Use one unchanged event question as the control.\n   140\t\n   141\t## 6. Not in scope\n   142\t\n   143\t- The judging, opening and extraction pieces (frozen).\n   144\t- The closed v13s line.\n   145\t- Other open defects.\n   146\t- No prompt or pipeline change.\n   147\t- The POC's own behaviour.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md'","aggregated_output":"     1\t# \"Forecast unavailable\" release, slice 1: built and checked at $0 (2026-11-23)\n     2\t\n     3\t**Result: accepted by council 75g** (`codex-r75g.md`), after rounds 75 to 75f. Slice 1 is built to `RELEASE-BUILD.md`:\n     4\t- revision 10 was ready per council 74j, after ten review rounds;\n     5\t- revision 11 records what councils 75 to 75f required of the build.\n     6\t\n     7\tIt passes its tests, its mutants and the $0 release check on four stored stores. Nothing is committed, published or deployed. The POC\n     8\tis unchanged; no POC code imports the release module.\n     9\t\n    10\t- Code: `src/hivemind/release.py`, `scripts/release_build.py`, `tests/test_release.py`.\n    11\t- Check: `release_check.py`; mutants: `release_mutants.py` (both in this folder).\n    12\t- Output: `poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23g/`. The runs `release-check-2026-11-23/` to `-23f/` predate later fixes and are kept for\n    13\t  the record. Their counts and bytes are the same; their seconds differ by run.\n    14\t- The mutant counts below come from separate runs of `release_mutants.py`, not from `results.json`.\n    15\t\n    16\t## 1. Council 75's findings, and what changed\n    17\t\n    18\tCouncil 75 (`codex-r75.md`) reproduced the four packages' counts and both refusals of the substituted forecast. It did not accept the\n    19\tslice. Its findings and the fixes:\n    20\t\n    21\t| Finding | Fix | Proof |\n    22\t|---|---|---|\n    23\t| A key written after the bound could reclassify an earlier package (the key lookup ignored its `seq`) | the key counts only when visible at the bound | test 22; mutant \"key read without its day\" |\n    24\t| Ten text fields accepted null, which revision 10 forbids | strings only | test 23; mutant \"null accepted as text\" |\n    25\t| `check` read the data file three times: it could hash one version and certify another | one read through one folder handle; hash and parse the same bytes; the command reports that data | structural (`check_package`) |\n    26\t| A path holding `%` could make SQLite open a different file from the one named | `release.store_path` refuses `%`, `?`, `#` | test 24; mutant \"store-path refusal removed\" |\n    27\t| Test 14's marker case supplied the very line its mutant removes | the instrumentation no longer touches the line that drops the staging path | test 14; mutant caught |\n    28\t| Test 13 damaged two things | the package copy keeps `e2` with no source, which is what a checker that drops missing items expects | test 13; mutant \"inner join\" caught |\n    29\t| Tests 1, 2 and 9 lacked decisive assertions | test 25 proves the writer's own refusal; test 2 checks all five labels in `v1`'s own fields; test 9 names each refusal's reason | mutants caught |\n    30\t| The mutant runner counted any non-zero exit | it stops on a failing control, and counts a catch only with a failing test and no setup or collection error | run below |\n    31\t| My first result overstated the closing check, the diagnostic search and the dated check, and the script never failed | corrected below; the script now fails on any missed acceptance item or budget | this run |\n    32\t\n    33\t**Council 75b** (`codex-r75b.md`) confirmed the fixes above and found four more gaps, now fixed:\n    34\t\n    35\t| Finding | Fix | Proof |\n    36\t|---|---|---|\n    37\t| The store-path check returned the original path, which the opener resolved again | `store_path` returns the resolved path, and the opener is given that | test 24 (a symbolic link); mutant \"store path returned unresolved\" |\n    38\t| A named pipe in a package would make `check` hang instead of refusing | files are opened without waiting (`O_NONBLOCK`), then refused by type | test 15, through the command with a 30 s bound; mutant \"pipe opened blocking\" |\n    39\t| The check script could pass with a required example missing | the three examples are a fixed list; a missing one fails the script | this run |\n    40\t| No test reordered records, and the runner credited a failure of a test's own scratch edit | test 10 reorders questions and evidence; scratch edits fail with \"scratch anchor\", which the runner does not count | mutant \"check_origins accepting another order\" |\n    41\t\n    42\tIt also asked that test 23 cover all ten text fields (now one case per field) and that test 2 check every question's own fields for\n    43\tthe labels (done).\n    44\t\n    45\t**Council 75c** (`codex-r75c.md`) found no off-list field or mismatched value, and judged every code finding of 75 and 75b closed. It\n    46\tfound three verification gaps, now fixed:\n    47\t\n    48\t| Finding | Fix | Proof |\n    49\t|---|---|---|\n    50\t| The runner read only pytest's short line, which can omit the \"scratch anchor\" message | each failure's full message is read from pytest's XML report | this run |\n    51\t| Test 2 skipped evidence fields; test 21 did not check that the whole report is printed | test 2 allows a `v1` label only in the fixture's known genuine source text; test 21 parses the printed report | mutants \"a number label written into another question's evidence\", \"report not printed\" |\n    52\t| The check script accepted an example id whose text had changed | superseded by council 75d's rule below | this run |\n    53\t\n    54\t**Council 75d** (`codex-r75d.md`) again found no off-list field or mismatched value. Its three findings had one mechanism:\n    55\t- test 2 took its \"genuine\" text from the export under test;\n    56\t- test 21 accepted a partial report;\n    57\t- the acceptance script's \"$390 billion\" also matches the system's own forecast, and a stale-hash refusal satisfied a check meant\n    58\t  for another reason.\n    59\t\n    60\t**One structural rule now holds** (AGENTS §1): every acceptance assertion compares against fixed expected values written down before\n    61\tthe run, never values taken from the output under test, and every refusal check matches its exact reason:\n    62\t- test 2 allows a label only in the fixture's own two constant texts;\n    63\t- tests 11 and 21 require the report's exact key set and fixed values;\n    64\t- the script compares each example's full summary and quote with the stored text written into it (old-1, 2026-11-23), and each\n    65\t  refusal with its exact message;\n    66\t- mutant \"report missing a field\" proves the key-set check.\n    67\t\n    68\t**Council 75e** (`codex-r75e.md`) found no path for a forbidden or mismatched value. It showed the rule was applied only partly, and it\n    69\tis now applied to the release tests' value and refusal assertions and to every check in the script:\n    70\t- the tests compare with literal key sets and the literal marker text, never the module's own constants;\n    71\t- test 2 checks each label occurrence by its location (question, evidence, field);\n    72\t- tests 11 and 21 check the report's full contents: counts `{number 5, event 1, Yes/No 1}`, 5 evidence, 6 sources, 101 fields\n    73\t  compared, 3,313 bytes, and the two unresolved questions with their reason;\n    74\t- every refusal of a value in the tests is matched by its exact message (some occupied-path tests check only the error type or exit\n    75\t  status; see the optional items below);\n    76\t- the script pins each store's day, classes and evidence count, the marker text, `v8`'s 1,284 pieces of evidence, the identity of the\n    77\t  forged value (the system's `j1580` forecast), both leak answers (\"Yes\"), the control (`v3`, \"Yes\") and the closing reason.\n    78\t\n    79\t**Council 75f** (`codex-r75f.md`) found two certification gaps and judged everything else optional under AGENTS §5. Both are fixed:\n    80\t- **Each dated package's own day is checked.** Before, a September package passed as the August one because both answers were \"Yes\".\n    81\t  Now the package and its manifest must carry the requested day, with the evidence count of that day: 2026-08-25, 3,239 pieces; \n    82\t  2026-08-28, 5,673 pieces.\n    83\t- **The delivered format and allow-list identifiers** (`hivemind-release/1`, `release-allow-list/1`) are compared with literal strings\n    84\t  in the script, for the data and manifest of every store, and in test 1. Before, they were compared only with the module's own\n    85\t  constants.\n    86\t\n    87\t**Left as optional (council 75f, AGENTS §5),** none of which lets a wrong package through:\n    88\t- a test helper takes its expected day from the export;\n    89\t- some occupied-path tests check only the error type or the exit status;\n    90\t- test 2's scan of other questions' evidence covers summaries and quotes; the origin check compares every field.\n    91\t\n    92\t**No regression.**\n    93\t- The release tests: 36 pass. The full suite passes: 425 tests, the frozen-ruler guards included.\n    94\t- Mutants: 31 of 32 are caught by failing tests, each judged from its full failure message (a failure of the test's own scratch edit\n    95\t  does not count), with no setup errors.\n    96\t- **The 32nd, the canonical-day check removed, is equivalent on this repository's Python 3.10.10,** whose `date.fromisoformat` already\n    97\t  refuses `20260825`. Under Python 3.13, on a temporary copy of `old-1` with one later completed day:\n    98\t  - the real code refuses `20260825`;\n    99\t  - the mutant exports `v8` with 1,284 pieces of evidence through 2026-09-20 into a package dated 2026-08-25, where the right package\n   100\t    holds 621.\n   101\t\n   102\t## 2. The $0 release check (design §7)\n   103\t\n   104\t| Store | Bound | Number / event / Yes-No | Evidence | Fields compared | Data bytes (library) | Seconds (library) |\n   105\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n   106\t| old-1 | 2026-09-20 | 19 / 28 / 0 | 8,251 | 91,055 | 5,788,634 (14,478,536) | 8.05 (6.36) |\n   107\t| old-2 | 2026-09-20 | 17 / 26 / 0 | 6,306 | 69,636 | 4,427,609 (11,893,701) | 6.19 (4.91) |\n   108\t| old-3 | 2026-09-20 | 18 / 31 / 0 | 6,659 | 73,559 | 4,685,247 (12,375,915) | 6.54 (5.25) |\n   109\t| served | 2026-08-28 | 13 / 55 / 0 | 6,461 | 71,524 | 4,612,321 (12,145,774) | 4.29 (3.36) |\n   110\t\n   111\t- **Every package passed its origin check:** every field compared with its stored source at the bound.\n   112\t- **No number question is unresolved** in these stores.\n   113\t- **Budgets met:**\n   114\t  - the bytes are 0.37–0.40 of the existing library's;\n   115\t  - the seconds are 1.25–1.28 times the library's, against a budget of 3 times and 120 s.\n   116\t- **How the evidence is counted.** The count includes each piece once per question that holds it. Every piece has exactly one source\n   117\t  row (`old-1`: 5,390 rows for 5,390 pieces).\n   118\t- **The script exits non-zero when any check it names fails:** each store's day, classes and evidence; the budgets; each example; each\n   119\t  exact refusal; the forged value's identity; `v8`; each leak; the control; the closing. This run ended \"every acceptance item and\n   120\t  budget met\".\n   121\t\n   122\t**The decisive acceptance case** (council 74, `old-1`):\n   123\t- **Kept, each equal to the store and to its full text written into the script before the run:**\n   124\t  - Morningstar's $361 billion (`e2295`, under `v8`);\n   125\t  - the genuine \"Bullish confirmation\" quote (`e1865`, under `v4`, `v5`, `v8`);\n   126\t  - the analysts' \"$390 billion\" (`e3597`, under `v4`, `v5`).\n   127\t- **The system's own forecast** (`j1580` implied outcome, \"About $390 billion: …\"):\n   128\t  - substituted into `e2295`'s summary, it is refused with exactly \"question v8.evidence e2295.one_line: differs from the store\";\n   129\t  - added to the manifest, it is refused with exactly \"the manifest: keys off the allow-list ['note'], missing []\".\n   130\t\n   131\t**The other checks:**\n   132\t- **`old-1/v8`:** class `number`, marked \"Forecast unavailable\". Its 1,284 pieces of evidence are the same ids as `service.evidence` at\n   133\t  the bound.\n   134\t- **The known Yes/No leaks at their own days.**\n   135\t  - `old-3/v36` at 2026-08-25 (judgement 799) and `old-1/v10` at 2026-08-28 (judgement 865) are the latest judgements there, and\n   136\t    each package carries its own day (3,239 and 5,673 pieces of evidence).\n   137\t  - Both keep \"Yes\".\n   138\t  - The full explanation and reason texts are absent.\n   139\t  - So are the judgements' own phrases: \"around $1 trillion\", \"rung 4\", \"at rung\" and \"capex at rung\" occur in no field.\n   140\t- **Control:** event `old-1/v3` keeps \"Yes\" and its evidence, equal to the store.\n   141\t- **Closing,** on a copy of `old-1` with a closing switch for `v8`, \"due 2026-09-20, frozen on 2026-09-20 at rung 2 Bullish\":\n   142\t  - `bundle.view_bundle` exposes it;\n   143\t  - the package shows `open: false`;\n   144\t  - the reason appears nowhere.\n   145\t  - The word \"Bullish\" does occur inside six `v8` fields: five source titles and the genuine `e1865` quote. That is source wording,\n   146\t    which the design keeps.\n   147\t\n   148\t## 3. The diagnostic search, every hit read\n   149\t\n   150\tThe search covered every decoded string of each package, ids, classes, the marker and the manifest included. For each question it\n   151\ttook every stored string the package must not hold:\n   152\t- rung labels of number questions;\n   153\t- the rung conditions of every question;\n   154\t- judgement reasons, explanations, implied outcomes and references, where the store has those columns (the served ledger lacks the\n   155\t  last two);\n   156\t- every switch reason, \"created\" included.\n   157\t\n   158\t| Store | Stored strings judged | Package strings | Hits |\n   159\t|---|---|---|---|\n   160\t| old-1 | 6,670 | 91,012 | 1,378: \"created\" 987, \"Bullish\" 391 |\n   161\t| old-2 | 6,677 | 69,597 | 771: \"created\" 516, \"Bullish\" 255 |\n   162\t| old-3 | 7,045 | 73,514 | 1,613: \"created\" 1,176, labels 437 (\"Bullish\", \"High\", \"Low\", \"Bearish\", \"Middle\") |\n   163\t| served | 2,149 | 71,460 | 1,794: \"created\" 1,632, \"Bullish\" 162 |\n   164\t\n   165\t- **No condition, reason, explanation, implied outcome, reference or closing reason is found anywhere.**\n   166\t- **The label hits are 257 package fields holding 32 distinct texts, all read.** Every one is source wording:\n   167\t  - headlines: \"Jensen Huang's Bullish Call …\", \"Stock Traded Lower\", \"Earnings Call Highlights\", \"Lows Not Seen Since 2019\",\n   168\t    \"Sky-High P/E\", \"That Bearish Bet\";\n   169\t  - the memory term \"High Bandwidth Memory\";\n   170\t  - the analyst quote \"Bullish confirmation would require …\".\n   171\t- **The \"created\" hits fall in 33 distinct texts, all containing the ordinary word.** It is every question's creation reason and\n   172\t  carries no forecast.\n   173\t\n   174\t## 4. Not shown, and still open\n   175\t\n   176\t- **The reader's screen** (slice 2, D756's screen check) is not built. The release page must read only this package, with no live\n   177\t  fetch and no idea submission, and needs a browser check of the `old-1/v8` screen.\n   178\t- **The idea path in the release:** deferred (council 74); its acceptance is pending.\n   179\t- **The recorded disagreement on evidence summaries** (`RELEASE-BUILD.md` §8) stands.\n   180\t- **`store.open_read_only` puts a path into a SQLite URI unescaped.** That is shared POC code; the release refuses such paths\n   181\t  rather than changing it.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py | sed -n '18,255p'\"","aggregated_output":"    18\tsys.path.insert(0, str(REPO / 'src'))\n    19\tfrom hivemind import bundle, release, service  # noqa: E402\n    20\tfrom hivemind.views import store  # noqa: E402\n    21\t\n    22\tCOMMAND = REPO / 'scripts' / 'release_build.py'\n    23\tMARKER = 'Forecast unavailable'                     # D726's words, written here, not read from the module under test\n    24\tFORMAT, ALLOW_LIST = 'hivemind-release/1', 'release-allow-list/1'   # revision 11's identifiers, written here, not read from the module\n    25\tDATED = {'old-3/v36@2026-08-25': ('2026-08-25', 3239), 'old-1/v10@2026-08-28': ('2026-08-28', 5673)}   # each dated package's day and evidence\n    26\tEXPECTED = {   # each store's default day, classes and evidence, fixed before this run from the reviewed first run (councils 75–75e reproduced them)\n    27\t    'old-1': ('2026-09-20', {'number': 19, 'event': 28, 'yes_no': 0}, 8251),\n    28\t    'old-2': ('2026-09-20', {'number': 17, 'event': 26, 'yes_no': 0}, 6306),\n    29\t    'old-3': ('2026-09-20', {'number': 18, 'event': 31, 'yes_no': 0}, 6659),\n    30\t    'served': ('2026-08-28', {'number': 13, 'event': 55, 'yes_no': 0}, 6461),\n    31\t}\n    32\tJ1580_PREFIX = 'About $390 billion: $164 billion reported in the first half'   # the system's own forecast used as the forged value\n    33\tCLOSING_REASON = 'due 2026-09-20, frozen on 2026-09-20 at rung 2 Bullish'\n    34\tCOMPARISON_ITEMS = REPO / 'poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/items-comparison.sqlite'\n    35\tSTORES = {\n    36\t    'old-1': (REPO / 'poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/views.sqlite', COMPARISON_ITEMS),\n    37\t    'old-2': (REPO / 'poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-2/prod/views.sqlite', COMPARISON_ITEMS),\n    38\t    'old-3': (REPO / 'poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-3/prod/views.sqlite', COMPARISON_ITEMS),\n    39\t    'served': (REPO / 'poc/data/served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/views.sqlite', REPO / 'poc/data/items-nvda-2026-07-01-10-27.sqlite'),\n    40\t}\n    41\t\n    42\t\n    43\tdef build(ledger, items, out, as_of=None):\n    44\t    args = [sys.executable, str(COMMAND), 'build', '--ledger', str(ledger), '--items', str(items), '--out', str(out)] + (['--as-of', as_of] if as_of else [])\n    45\t    result = subprocess.run(args, capture_output=True, text=True, env={'PATH': '/usr/bin:/bin', 'PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE': '1'})\n    46\t    if result.returncode != 0:\n    47\t        raise SystemExit(f'build {out} exited {result.returncode}: {result.stderr}')\n    48\t    return json.loads(out.with_name(out.name + '.report.json').read_text()), release.read_data(out)\n    49\t\n    50\t\n    51\tdef check(ledger, items, package):\n    52\t    views_db, items_db = service.open_ledger(str(ledger)), store.open_read_only(str(items))\n    53\t    try:\n    54\t        return release.check_package(package, views_db, items_db)[0]\n    55\t    finally:\n    56\t        views_db.close()\n    57\t        items_db.close()\n    58\t\n    59\t\n    60\tdef fields(data, manifest=None):\n    61\t    \"\"\"(question id, field path, evidence id, text) for every decoded string of the package: every string value of the data at\n    62\t    every level (ids, classes and the marker included) and of the manifest.\"\"\"\n    63\t    def walk(value, path, question_id, evidence_id):\n    64\t        if isinstance(value, dict):\n    65\t            question_id = value['id'] if 'class' in value else question_id\n    66\t            evidence_id = value['id'] if 'one_line' in value else evidence_id\n    67\t            for key, item in value.items():\n    68\t                yield from walk(item, f'{path}.{key}' if path else key, question_id, evidence_id)\n    69\t        elif isinstance(value, list):\n    70\t            for n, item in enumerate(value):\n    71\t                yield from walk(item, f'{path}[{n}]', question_id, evidence_id)\n    72\t        elif isinstance(value, str):\n    73\t            yield question_id, path, evidence_id, value\n    74\t    yield from walk(data, '', None, None)\n    75\t    if manifest is not None:\n    76\t        yield from walk(manifest, 'manifest', None, None)\n    77\t\n    78\t\n    79\tdef forbidden(ledger, data):\n    80\t    \"\"\"Every stored string the package must not hold, by question and kind; judgement columns read only where the store has them.\"\"\"\n    81\t    conn = service.open_ledger(str(ledger))\n    82\t    try:\n    83\t        columns = {row[1] for row in conn.execute('pragma table_info(judgements)')}\n    84\t        texts = [c for c in ('reasons', 'why_changed', 'implied_outcome', 'reference') if c in columns]\n    85\t        out = []\n    86\t        for question in data['questions']:\n    87\t            view_id = question['id']\n    88\t            for row in conn.execute('select label, condition from rungs where view_id=?', (view_id,)):\n    89\t                if question['class'] == 'number':                # an event's or Yes/No question's labels are its shown answers\n    90\t                    out.append((view_id, 'rung label', row['label']))\n    91\t                out.append((view_id, 'rung condition', row['condition']))\n    92\t            for row in conn.execute(f'select {\", \".join(texts)} from judgements where view_id=?', (view_id,)):\n    93\t                out += [(view_id, name, row[name]) for name in texts]\n    94\t            out += [(view_id, 'switch reason', row['reason']) for row in conn.execute('select reason from view_switches where view_id=?', (view_id,))]\n    95\t        return [entry for entry in out if entry[2]], [c for c in ('implied_outcome', 'reference') if c not in columns]\n    96\t    finally:\n    97\t        conn.close()\n    98\t\n    99\t\n   100\tdef diagnostics(ledger, data, package):\n   101\t    stored, absent = forbidden(ledger, data)\n   102\t    located = list(fields(data, json.loads((package / release.MANIFEST_FILE).read_text())))\n   103\t    joined = '\\x00'.join(text for *_, text in located)\n   104\t    hits = []\n   105\t    for view_id, kind, text in set(stored):\n   106\t        if text in joined:\n   107\t            for question_id, path, evidence_id, field in located:\n   108\t                if text in field:\n   109\t                    hits.append({'stored_in': view_id, 'kind': kind, 'text': text[:200], 'found_in': question_id, 'field': path, 'evidence': evidence_id})\n   110\t    return {'stored_strings_judged': len(set(stored)), 'package_strings': len(located), 'judgement_columns_absent': absent, 'hits': hits}\n   111\t\n   112\t\n   113\tdef library_baseline(ledger, items):\n   114\t    views_db, items_db = service.open_ledger(str(ledger)), store.open_read_only(str(items))\n   115\t    try:\n   116\t        started = time.monotonic()\n   117\t        payload = bundle.library(views_db, items_db)\n   118\t        return len(json.dumps(payload, ensure_ascii=False).encode()), time.monotonic() - started\n   119\t    finally:\n   120\t        views_db.close()\n   121\t        items_db.close()\n   122\t\n   123\t\n   124\tdef by_id(data):\n   125\t    return {q['id']: q for q in data['questions']}\n   126\t\n   127\t\n   128\tdef refresh(package, data=None, manifest_extra=None):\n   129\t    if data is not None:\n   130\t        payload = json.dumps(data, ensure_ascii=False, separators=(',', ':')).encode()\n   131\t        (package / release.DATA_FILE).write_bytes(payload)\n   132\t    manifest = json.loads((package / release.MANIFEST_FILE).read_text())\n   133\t    manifest['data_sha256'] = hashlib.sha256((package / release.DATA_FILE).read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n   134\t    manifest.update(manifest_extra or {})\n   135\t    (package / release.MANIFEST_FILE).write_text(json.dumps(manifest))\n   136\t\n   137\t\n   138\tdef refused(ledger, items, package):\n   139\t    try:\n   140\t        check(ledger, items, package)\n   141\t    except release.ReleaseRefused as error:\n   142\t        return str(error)\n   143\t    return None\n   144\t\n   145\t\n   146\tdef main(out):\n   147\t    out = Path(out).absolute()\n   148\t    out.mkdir()                                            # a new folder; refuses an existing one\n   149\t    results = {'stores': {}}\n   150\t    packages = {}\n   151\t    for name, (ledger, items) in STORES.items():\n   152\t        (out / name).mkdir()\n   153\t        report, data = build(ledger, items, out / name / 'package')\n   154\t        packages[name] = data\n   155\t        library_bytes, library_seconds = library_baseline(ledger, items)\n   156\t        seconds = report['export_seconds'] + report['check_seconds']\n   157\t        results['stores'][name] = {\n   158\t            'as_of': report['as_of'], 'counts': report['counts'], 'withheld_unresolved': len(report['withheld_unresolved']),\n   159\t            'unresolved': report['withheld_unresolved'], 'data_bytes': report['data_bytes'], 'library_bytes': library_bytes,\n   160\t            'seconds': round(seconds, 2), 'library_seconds': round(library_seconds, 2),\n   161\t            'bytes_within_budget': report['data_bytes'] <= library_bytes,\n   162\t            'seconds_within_budget': seconds <= 3 * library_seconds and seconds <= 120,\n   163\t            'diagnostics': diagnostics(ledger, data, out / name / 'package')}\n   164\t        print(name, json.dumps({k: v for k, v in results['stores'][name].items() if k not in ('unresolved', 'diagnostics')}), 'hits', len(results['stores'][name]['diagnostics']['hits']))\n   165\t\n   166\t    ledger, items = STORES['old-1']\n   167\t    data, package = packages['old-1'], out / 'old-1' / 'package'\n   168\t    conn = service.open_ledger(str(ledger))\n   169\t    stored = {row['evidence_id']: row for row in conn.execute(\"select * from evidence where evidence_id in ('e2295','e1865','e3597')\")}\n   170\t    implied = conn.execute('select implied_outcome from judgements where judgement_id=1580').fetchone()[0]\n   171\t    in_force_v8 = [e['evidence_id'] for e in service.evidence(conn, 'v8', data['as_of'])]\n   172\t    conn.close()\n   173\t    required_text = {   # each example's full stored text, written down before the run (old-1, 2026-11-23); compared exactly\n   174\t        'e2295': ('Morningstar cites NVIDIA Data Center revenue of $3 billion in FY2020 and $194 billion in FY2026, and estimates $361 billion in FY2027, up 86% year over year.',\n   175\t                  'Nvidia’s DC business has achieved exponential growth already, rising from $3 billion in fiscal 2020 to $194 billion in fiscal 2026, and we estimate it will be $361 billion in fiscal 2027, representing 86% annual growth.'),\n   176\t        'e1865': ('The author identifies firm SpaceX procurement commitments and NVIDIA Data Center growth above 60% into FY2028 as bullish confirmation conditions.',\n   177\t                  'Bullish confirmation would require firm procurement commitments for the SpaceX buildout and continued NVIDIA Data Center growth above 60% into fiscal 2028.'),\n   178\t        'e3597': ('The author says analysts estimate NVIDIA revenue of about $390 billion in calendar 2027 and over $550 billion in calendar 2028, with annual sales growth of roughly 24% to 25%.',\n   179\t                  'Analysts see revenue reaching about $390 billion in 2027 and more than $550 billion in 2028, with annual sales growth of roughly 24% to 25%.')}\n   180\t    kept = {}\n   181\t    for evidence_id in ('e2295', 'e1865', 'e3597'):              # the fixed examples: a missing one is a failure, not a smaller list\n   182\t        if evidence_id not in stored:\n   183\t            kept[evidence_id] = {'questions': [], 'equal_to_store': False, 'present': False}\n   184\t            continue\n   185\t        holders = [(q['id'], e) for q in data['questions'] for e in q['evidence'] if e['id'] == evidence_id]\n   186\t        kept[evidence_id] = {'questions': [h[0] for h in holders],\n   187\t                             'equal_to_store': all(e['one_line'] == stored[evidence_id]['one_line'] and e['quote'] == stored[evidence_id]['quote'] for _, e in holders) and bool(holders),\n   188\t                             'present': bool(holders),\n   189\t                             'holds_its_wording': bool(holders) and all((e['one_line'], e['quote']) == required_text[evidence_id] for _, e in holders)}\n   190\t    forged = out / 'old-1' / 'forged-summary'\n   191\t    shutil.copytree(package, forged)\n   192\t    changed = json.loads(json.dumps(data))\n   193\t    next(e for e in by_id(changed)['v8']['evidence'] if e['id'] == 'e2295')['one_line'] = implied\n   194\t    refresh(forged, changed)\n   195\t    prose = out / 'old-1' / 'forged-manifest'\n   196\t    shutil.copytree(package, prose)\n   197\t    refresh(prose, manifest_extra={'note': implied})\n   198\t    v8 = by_id(data)['v8']\n   199\t    results['decisive'] = {'kept': kept, 'implied_outcome_j1580': implied[:120],\n   200\t                           'substituted_into_e2295_refused': refused(ledger, items, forged),\n   201\t                           'added_to_manifest_refused': refused(ledger, items, prose),\n   202\t                           'unchanged_package_passes': check(ledger, items, package)['fields_compared']}\n   203\t    results['decisive']['forged_value_is_j1580'] = implied.startswith(J1580_PREFIX)\n   204\t    results['old-1/v8'] = {'class': v8['class'], 'forecast': v8['forecast'], 'evidence': len(v8['evidence']),\n   205\t                           'same_ids_as_service_evidence': [e['id'] for e in v8['evidence']] == in_force_v8}\n   206\t\n   207\t    leaks = {}\n   208\t    for name, view_id, day, judgement_id in (('old-3', 'v36', '2026-08-25', 799), ('old-1', 'v10', '2026-08-28', 865)):\n   209\t        ledger, items = STORES[name]\n   210\t        report, dated = build(ledger, items, out / name / f'package-{day}', day)\n   211\t        conn = service.open_ledger(str(ledger))\n   212\t        row = conn.execute('select judgement_id, rung, why_changed, reasons from judgements where view_id=? and publication_day<=? order by judgement_id desc limit 1', (view_id, day)).fetchone()\n   213\t        label = conn.execute('select label from rungs where view_id=? and position=?', (view_id, row['rung'])).fetchone()[0]\n   214\t        conn.close()\n   215\t        record = by_id(dated)[view_id]\n   216\t        dated_manifest = json.loads((out / name / f'package-{day}' / release.MANIFEST_FILE).read_text())\n   217\t        texts = [text for *_, text in fields(dated)]\n   218\t        leaks[f'{name}/{view_id}@{day}'] = {\n   219\t            'package_as_of': dated['as_of'], 'manifest_as_of': dated_manifest['as_of'], 'evidence': report['counts']['evidence'],\n   220\t            'latest_judgement': row['judgement_id'], 'expected_judgement': judgement_id, 'label_kept': record['answer'] == label, 'answer': record['answer'],\n   221\t            'why_changed_absent': not any(row['why_changed'] in t for t in texts), 'reasons_absent': not any((row['reasons'] or '\\x01') in t for t in texts),\n   222\t            'phrase_fields': {phrase: [(q, p, e, t[:160]) for q, p, e, t in fields(dated) if phrase in t]\n   223\t                              for phrase in ('around $1 trillion', 'rung 4', 'at rung', 'capex at rung')}}\n   224\t    results['leaks'] = leaks\n   225\t\n   226\t    ledger, items = STORES['old-1']\n   227\t    conn = service.open_ledger(str(ledger))\n   228\t    control = next(q for q in data['questions'] if q['class'] == 'event' and q['id'] not in ('v10',) and q['answer'] is not None)\n   229\t    stored_label = conn.execute('select r.label from judgements j join rungs r on r.view_id=j.view_id and r.position=j.rung where j.view_id=? and j.publication_day<=? order by j.judgement_id desc limit 1', (control['id'], data['as_of'])).fetchone()[0]\n   230\t    control_ids = [e['evidence_id'] for e in service.evidence(conn, control['id'], data['as_of'])]\n   231\t    conn.close()\n   232\t    results['control'] = {'id': control['id'], 'answer': control['answer'], 'label_equals_store': control['answer'] == stored_label,\n   233\t                          'evidence_equals_store': [e['id'] for e in control['evidence']] == control_ids}\n   234\t\n   235\t    closing = out / 'old-1' / 'closing'\n   236\t    closing.mkdir()\n   237\t    copy = closing / 'views.sqlite'\n   238\t    shutil.copyfile(ledger, copy)\n   239\t    conn = sqlite3.connect(copy)\n   240\t    rung = conn.execute(\"select rung from judgements where view_id='v8' order by judgement_id desc limit 1\").fetchone()[0]\n   241\t    rung_label = conn.execute(\"select label from rungs where view_id='v8' and position=?\", (rung,)).fetchone()[0]\n   242\t    reason = f'due {data[\"as_of\"]}, frozen on {data[\"as_of\"]} at rung {rung} {rung_label}'\n   243\t    last_seq = conn.execute('select max(sequence_no) from processing_steps').fetchone()[0]\n   244\t    conn.execute(\"insert into view_switches (view_id, open, reason, by_whom, after_seq) values ('v8', 0, ?, 'pull', ?)\", (reason, last_seq))\n   245\t    conn.commit()\n   246\t    conn.close()\n   247\t    views_db, items_db = service.open_ledger(str(copy)), store.open_read_only(str(items))\n   248\t    exposed = bundle.view_bundle(views_db, bundle.item_lookup(items_db), 'v8')\n   249\t    views_db.close()\n   250\t    items_db.close()\n   251\t    report, closed = build(copy, items, closing / 'package')\n   252\t    texts = [text for *_, text in fields(closed)]\n   253\t    results['closing'] = {'reason': reason, 'bundle_exposes_reason': any(s.get('reason') == reason for s in exposed['switches']),\n   254\t                          'package_open': by_id(closed)['v8']['open'], 'reason_absent': not any(reason in t for t in texts),\n   255\t                          'rung_label_inside_v8_fields': [(p, e, t[:120]) for q, p, e, t in fields(closed) if q == 'v8' and rung_label in t]}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
