{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"ls -l poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23g && rg -n 'FORMAT|ALLOW_LIST|evidence|source|as_of' src/hivemind/release.py | head -125\"","aggregated_output":"total 2216\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 9 lchingen  staff      288 Nov 23 11:34 old-1\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 4 lchingen  staff      128 Nov 23 11:33 old-2\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 6 lchingen  staff      192 Nov 23 11:33 old-3\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff  1130609 Nov 23 11:34 results.json\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 4 lchingen  staff      128 Nov 23 11:33 served\n4:A number question carries its question, its evidence in force and the marker \"Forecast unavailable\". An event or Yes/No question\n5:carries its question, its evidence and its answer labels. Nothing else is read into the package: no rung condition or bound, no\n7:stored source at the package's day, and nothing published replaces an existing path.\n24:FORMAT = 'hivemind-release/1'\n25:ALLOW_LIST = 'release-allow-list/1'\n32:    'envelope': frozenset({'format', 'allow_list', 'as_of', 'questions'}),\n33:    'number': frozenset({'id', 'question', 'open', 'class', 'forecast', 'evidence'}),\n34:    'answered': frozenset({'id', 'question', 'open', 'class', 'answers', 'answer', 'evidence'}),\n35:    'evidence': frozenset({'id', 'one_line', 'quote', 'tier', 'speaker', 'original_who', 'original_day', 'sources'}),\n36:    'source': frozenset({'title', 'publisher', 'day', 'uri'}),\n37:    'manifest': frozenset({'format', 'allow_list', 'as_of', 'data_sha256'}),\n64:def resolve(views_db, as_of=None):\n67:    if as_of is not None:\n68:        canonical_day(as_of)\n69:    bound = service.resolve_bound(views_db, as_of)\n81:def key_measure(conn, view_id, as_of):\n87:    return row['measure'] if row is not None and service.visible(conn, row['seq'], as_of) else None\n95:def question_class(conn, view_id, labels, as_of):\n99:    if key_measure(conn, view_id, as_of) in identity.EVENT_MEASURES:\n106:def _answer(conn, view_id, as_of, positions):\n108:    row = conn.execute('select rung from judgements where view_id=? and publication_day<=? order by judgement_id desc limit 1', (view_id, as_of)).fetchone()\n118:def _item(items_db, cache, input_id, evidence_id):\n120:        row = items_db.execute('select title, publisher, source_uri from items where input_id=?', (input_id,)).fetchone()\n122:            raise ReleaseRefused(f'evidence {evidence_id}: source item {input_id} is not in the items database')\n127:def _visible_views(conn, as_of):\n128:    return [row for row in conn.execute('select view_id, question, created_seq from views order by created_seq, rowid') if service.visible(conn, row['created_seq'], as_of)]\n131:def release_export(views_db, items_db, as_of=None):\n135:        bound = resolve(views_db, as_of)\n142:            record = {'id': view_id, 'question': view['question'], 'open': service.is_open_as_of(views_db, view_id, bound), 'class': kind}\n148:            evidence = []\n149:            for piece in service.evidence(views_db, view_id, bound):\n150:                sources = []\n151:                for source in piece['sources']:\n152:                    item = _item(items_db, items, source['input_id'], piece['evidence_id'])\n153:                    sources.append({'title': item['title'], 'publisher': item['publisher'], 'day': source['publication_day'], 'uri': item['source_uri']})\n154:                evidence.append({'id': piece['evidence_id'], **{name: piece[name] for name in EVIDENCE_TEXT}, 'sources': sources})\n155:            record['evidence'] = evidence\n157:        data = {'format': FORMAT, 'allow_list': ALLOW_LIST, 'as_of': bound, 'questions': questions}\n182:    if data['format'] != FORMAT or data['allow_list'] != ALLOW_LIST:\n184:    canonical_day(data['as_of'])\n187:    counts = {'questions': {kind: 0 for kind in CLASSES}, 'evidence': 0, 'sources': 0}\n207:        if not isinstance(question['evidence'], list):\n208:            raise ReleaseRefused(f'{where}: evidence is not a list')\n209:        for piece in question['evidence']:\n210:            _keys(piece, 'evidence', f'{where} evidence')\n211:            _texts(piece, ('id',), f'{where} evidence')\n212:            _texts(piece, EVIDENCE_TEXT, f'{where} evidence {piece[\"id\"]}')\n213:            if not isinstance(piece['sources'], list):\n214:                raise ReleaseRefused(f'{where} evidence {piece[\"id\"]}: sources is not a list')\n215:            for source in piece['sources']:\n216:                _keys(source, 'source', f'{where} evidence {piece[\"id\"]} source')\n217:                _texts(source, SOURCE_TEXT, f'{where} evidence {piece[\"id\"]} source')\n218:            counts['sources'] += len(piece['sources'])\n219:        counts['evidence'] += len(question['evidence'])\n226:def _open_at(conn, view_id, as_of):\n228:        if service.visible(conn, row['after_seq'], as_of):\n233:def _expected_evidence(views_db, items_db, view_id, as_of):\n234:    \"\"\"The evidence in force at the day, by its own SQL: visible links in link order, minus those whose latest replacement is\n235:    visible; each source row visible at the day, in row order, with its item required.\"\"\"\n237:    for link in views_db.execute('select evidence_id, seq from evidence_links where view_id=? order by id', (view_id,)).fetchall():\n238:        if not service.visible(views_db, link['seq'], as_of):\n240:        latest = views_db.execute('select seq from replacements where old_evidence_id=? order by id desc limit 1', (link['evidence_id'],)).fetchone()\n241:        if latest is not None and service.visible(views_db, latest['seq'], as_of):\n243:        row = views_db.execute(f'select evidence_id, {\", \".join(EVIDENCE_TEXT)} from evidence where evidence_id=?', (link['evidence_id'],)).fetchone()\n245:            raise ReleaseRefused(f'{view_id}: link to evidence {link[\"evidence_id\"]}, which the store does not hold')\n246:        sources = []\n247:        for source in views_db.execute('select input_id, publication_day, seq from evidence_sources where evidence_id=? order by id', (link['evidence_id'],)).fetchall():\n248:            if not service.visible(views_db, source['seq'], as_of):\n250:            item = items_db.execute('select title, publisher, source_uri from items where input_id=?', (source['input_id'],)).fetchone()\n252:                raise ReleaseRefused(f'evidence {row[\"evidence_id\"]}: source item {source[\"input_id\"]} is not in the items database')\n253:            sources.append({'title': item['title'], 'publisher': item['publisher'], 'day': source['publication_day'], 'uri': item['source_uri']})\n254:        out.append({'id': row['evidence_id'], **{name: row[name] for name in EVIDENCE_TEXT}, 'sources': sources})\n281:def check_origins(views_db, items_db, data, expected_as_of):\n282:    \"\"\"Every package field against its permitted stored source at `expected_as_of`, derived from the store and never from the\n283:    package: the day, each question's class, the questions, evidence and sources in order with their counts. Its reads are its own\n287:        as_of = canonical_day(expected_as_of)\n288:        if data['as_of'] != as_of:\n289:            raise ReleaseRefused(f'the package is dated {data[\"as_of\"]}, the store bound is {as_of}')\n291:                 if service.visible(views_db, row['created_seq'], as_of)]\n296:        compared = _compare(FORMAT, data['format'], 'package.format') + _compare(ALLOW_LIST, data['allow_list'], 'package.allow_list') + 1\n301:            kind = question_class(views_db, view_id, labels, as_of)\n302:            record = {'id': view_id, 'question': view['question'], 'open': _open_at(views_db, view_id, as_of), 'class': kind}\n306:                latest = views_db.execute('select rung from judgements where view_id=? and publication_day<=? order by judgement_id desc limit 1', (view_id, as_of)).fetchone()\n311:            expected_evidence = _expected_evidence(views_db, items_db, view_id, as_of)\n312:            if not isinstance(question.get('evidence'), list) or len(question['evidence']) != len(expected_evidence):\n313:                found = len(question['evidence']) if isinstance(question.get('evidence'), list) else 'no'\n314:                raise ReleaseRefused(f'question {view_id}.evidence: {found} entries where the store has {len(expected_evidence)}')\n315:            record['evidence'] = question['evidence']           # compared piece by piece below, named by the stored evidence id\n316:            compared += _compare(record, question, f'question {view_id}') - _leaves(question['evidence'])\n317:            for expected, actual in zip(expected_evidence, question['evidence']):\n318:                compared += _compare(expected, actual, f'question {view_id}.evidence {expected[\"id\"]}')\n338:    manifest = {'format': data['format'], 'allow_list': data['allow_list'], 'as_of': data['as_of'], 'data_sha256': hashlib.sha256(payload).hexdigest()}\n347:        return lambda source, target: call(source, target, RENAME_EXCL)\n351:        return lambda source, target: call(AT_FDCWD, source, AT_FDCWD, target, RENAME_NOREPLACE)\n442:def check_package(path, views_db=None, items_db=None, expected_as_of=None):\n445:    parsed; data that passes `check_export` and, with the stores, `check_origins` at `expected_as_of` (or at the package's own day\n466:    for name in ('format', 'allow_list', 'as_of'):\n470:        bound = expected_as_of if expected_as_of is not None else resolve(views_db, data['as_of'])\n486:            out.append({'id': question['id'], 'reason': reason, 'has_key': key_measure(views_db, question['id'], data['as_of']) is not None})\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,43p' docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md && rg -n 'D75[6-9]|slice 2|76b' docs/{CURRENT_STATE.md,DECISIONS-log.md} | tail -32\"","aggregated_output":"# Core PRD for the next phase: filing must recognise indirect relations the way an analyst does\n\n> Status: in progress (opened 2026-11-04). Alex: \"你把这个写好成下一阶段核心PRD然后不要drift, 把所有需要的context 全部充分记录，每次开始前都需要revisit, 然后开始做\".\n> This page is the single source for this phase. In a conflict: Alex's words → `docs/DECISIONS.md` → this page → the other design documents. This page's\n> conclusions, evidence, constraints, measuring method and process are not rewritten to follow test results;\n> test results go into `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/log.md`, and changing this page first needs Alex's word.\n> Amended 2026-11-04 (Alex replied \"go\" to the proposed amendment; D360): §5.2 drops \"also file under the other party's question\" and puts two\n> sentences in its place, one on choosing and one on splitting; §6's decision rule is rewritten. How it came about:\n> `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/prd-amendment-proposal.md` and `log.md` rows 11–16.\n> 2026-11-05 (D368): translated into English on Alex's word (\"不，用英文吧\"); §4 corrected to name the frozen standard's version 5 and §5 given a status line, on his delegation (\"你要来帮我看到底做不做\").\n\n## 0. Checklist before every start (Alex: \"每次开始前都需要revisit\")\n\nBefore starting any step, finish these in order; if one cannot be done, do not start:\n\n1. Read §§1–8 of this page in full; read the last three rows of `log.md`, and confirm where the previous step stopped and why.\n2. Check against §3, \"not in scope\": what this step does is not in that table. If it is in the table, stop and take it to Alex.\n3. Check against §4, \"constraints\": this step changes nothing frozen; a change to the frozen extraction prompt is the one place §5 names, and Alex's\n   word for it is already given.\n4. If this step costs money: its predictions and stop conditions are written down and frozen as §7 says (with their sha256 recorded beside them); the\n   requests are rebuilt byte for byte as §6 says; the control is re-sent the same day.\n5. What goes to Alex: one conclusion, one recommendation, one test, after §7's rounds of review; no menu of options; in plain words (the opening of\n   AGENTS, \"Explain and answer as to a sixteen-year-old\").\n\n## 1. Goal (end to end)\n\nEach question's judgement must receive the facts that can change its answer; facts that no question receives, those that bear on no question, must\nnot be piled into some one question. What is measured is the final judgement (the frozen judgement ruler, reader B, at the window end 2026-07-14), not\nany one step's own score.\n\n## 2. The core blocker (proven)\n\n**The system uses a fact for a question only when the fact \"states exactly this question's own figure\". An analyst also reasons onward from a fact: the other party's figure in a deal, price and volume for a product's revenue, a product's variants for its launch, and so on. The filing step cannot do this; the judging step reasons onward once it has the facts.**\n\nThis one blocker has two faces (described earlier as \"two problems\"):\n\n- **The parking lot.** Filing does not recognise facts that bear on a question indirectly, so no question takes them; yet to be kept, a fact must\n  first be filed (D209, D264). So D273 added the fallback sentence, which parks them in NVIDIA's total-revenue question. Of the reports under the\n  total-revenue question, in the part the gold read, 32–39% are ones the standard does not keep, 31–44% are kept but used by none of the 22 questions,\n  and only 7–10% are what the gold actually uses to judge total revenue (three draws); 24–44% of the total-revenue question's judgement citations are\n  news about other companies or the whole market (Intel graphics-card retail prices, a gas-fired power plant in Taiwan).\n- **Narrow questions starve.** Questions that only indirect facts can answer do not receive them: the custom-chip question received none of Broadcom's\n  figures in any of the three draws, and judged \"below $40 billion\" in all three; the operating-margin and NVIDIA capital-spending questions received\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md:448:**The one next task: slice 2 of the \"Forecast unavailable\" release, the reader's screen (D758 order; D756's screen check).** The release\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md:453:**Slice 1 is built and accepted at $0 (D759).**\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md:471:The record of the D758 step:\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md:473:**Earlier next task (done, D759): build slice 1 once its design passes council 74 (D758).**\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md:475:The record of the D757 step:\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md:477:**Earlier next task (done, D758): Alex chooses whether to open release work, and what non-number questions show (D757).** Decided by\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md:478:council 73 under D439 (D758): open, and (a).\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md:480:The record of the D756 step:\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md:482:**Earlier next task (done, D757): when release work opens, a $0 check of the reader's screen for number questions (D756).** On a\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md:486:- **Alex closed the v13s judge line at its STOP** (D756: end the line, release with \"Forecast unavailable\"). Nothing from it enters the\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md:492:**Earlier next task (done, D756): Alex reads the paid re-send's STOP (D755) and confirms the council's recommendation.** The\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md:881:  - stage 0 and slice 2;\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:9763:      not eligible. On slice 2: 156 of 156 and 79 of 79;\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:9877:  - **The setup:** scratch copies of slice 2 relabelled as the six draws, keys in a scratch folder, and a fake reader.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:11823:## D756 · 2026-11-23 · Alex closes the v13s line; the first release shows number questions as \"Forecast unavailable\"\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:11842:## D757 · 2026-11-23 · Toward production: the \"Forecast unavailable\" release design is ready for when Alex opens release work (council 72–72d); two choices go to Alex\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:11845:  unavailable\" (D756). D726 says it \"is built with the release work, which is not started\". Council 72 agreed that opening release\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:11867:## D758 · 2026-11-23 · Under D439 the council opens local release work for \"Forecast unavailable\"; non-number questions show no explanation text (§4 a); the v13s checker defects are closed as won't-fix (council 73)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:11870:  Production 方向去走了\"). He had already chosen the behaviour (D726 \"同意\"; D756 \"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线\"). D757 left two\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:11880:     code, the line is closed (D756), and the STOP bars tuning on the 36 answers. The findings stay on record.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:11881:  4. **Order:** the exporter and the checked package first; the reader's screen second (it completes D756's screen check). How the\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:11885:## D759 · 2026-11-23 · Slice 1 of the \"Forecast unavailable\" release is built and accepted at $0 (councils 74–74j design, 75–75g build); nothing committed or published\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:11887:- **Under D439 and D758.** Release work was opened by council 73 (D758). This slice carries it out locally at $0. Nothing is\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:11895:    Yes/No question carries its question, evidence and answer labels (D758 §4 a);\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:11926:  - slice 2, the release page that reads only the package, with a browser check of the `old-1/v8` screen (D756's screen check);\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md | sed -n '50,165p'\nnl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '11830,11912p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md | sed -n '50,165p'\nnl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '11830,11912p'\"","aggregated_output":"    50\t  - the marker \"Forecast unavailable\".\n    51\t\n    52\t  Nothing else is listed:\n    53\t  - no ladder;\n    54\t  - no band, label or condition;\n    55\t  - no reasons or why_changed;\n    56\t  - no history, counts or assessment dates;\n    57\t  - no closing band (\"closed\" only);\n    58\t  - no theme pushes, no composite, no idea derived from its forecast.\n    59\t- **Ideas.** The release's idea composition (`idea.py`, `idea_composite.py`) runs on export data only. A number question enters it\n    60\t  as question and evidence with the marker. Its ladder is not read from storage in either the answer-format build or the summary\n    61\t  input (`idea_composite.py:255`, `:281`; `poc-v118-idea.json:94`). The test inspects the composed request itself, not only the\n    62\t  delivered card.\n    63\t- **The POC is unchanged.** Its API, MCP and page keep today's behaviour. Whether colleagues' POC page also changes is a separate\n    64\t  later choice for Alex.\n    65\t\n    66\t## 3. Identity: what a number question is (verified on four stores by council 72b)\n    67\t\n    68\tA view is a number question unless one of the following excludes it:\n    69\t1. **An event.** The view key's measure is in `identity.EVENT_MEASURES` (`event`, `policy_event`). That covers 85 of 85 event\n    70\t   questions in the three comparison stores.\n    71\t2. **A Yes/No question.** The ladder has exactly two labels which, canonicalised with the existing vocabulary\n    72\t   (`vocabulary.canonical`), are Yes and No in either order. The sealed ledger's 30 such questions use `是` and `否`. The Xbox `v37`\n    73\t   (`growth_rate`, bounds around zero) is Yes/No.\n    74\t\n    75\tEvery other view is a number question. Its forecast is withheld whether its bands come from `lo`/`hi`, parse from the conditions\n    76\t(the sealed `v3`), or cannot be resolved. An unresolved record is withheld and listed in the release check, with a key or without\n    77\t(council 72b: an `old-1/v8` copy without bounds does not parse, and its key still exists).\n    78\t\n    79\tCounts (council 72b), number / event or Yes/No:\n    80\t- `old-1` 19 / 28, `old-2` 17 / 26, `old-3` 18 / 31;\n    81\t- the sealed ledger: 43 parse as money, 21 are withheld as unresolved, 30 are Yes/No.\n    82\t\n    83\tNo wrong show-or-withhold result was found.\n    84\t\n    85\t**Events are binary too.** All 85 comparison-store events are also two-answer questions, including both known prose leaks, and a\n    86\tbinary event such as \"Restriction adopted\" / \"No restriction adopted\" exists in the served ledger (council 72c). §4's rule applies to\n    87\tevery question that is not a number question, events and Yes/No alike, and each keeps its answer label.\n    88\t\n    89\t## 4. Questions that are not number questions: an open choice for Alex (not decided here)\n    90\t\n    91\tD726 covers number questions. A Yes/No question's band is not a number forecast, but its stored explanation can quote one (§1). The\n    92\tallow-list must say which Yes/No fields the release shows:\n    93\t- **(a)** the question, its evidence and its answer (Yes/No and label), with no explanation text. Safe, and it removes the reasoning\n    94\t  readers would see.\n    95\t- **(b)** as (a), plus the explanation only for judgements whose request showed the judge no number question's state. Code can\n    96\t  decide this from the stored request (`views/judging.py`, which builds the related questions shown).\n    97\t- **Measured (council 72c),** matching each judgement to its archived request:\n    98\t  - (b) would keep explanations on 31 of 769, 44 of 776 and 43 of 958 judgements in the three comparison runs;\n    99\t  - for a reader at the latest answer, it would keep them on 21 of 85 questions;\n   100\t  - it would keep 73 of 73 in the sealed ledger.\n   101\t- **The limit of (b).** It cannot promise the prose quotes no number forecast. A request also carries the question's own previous\n   102\t  reasoning, and can carry another question's, either of which may repeat a forecast seen earlier. Both known leaks are in\n   103\t  `why_changed`.\n   104\t- **Recommendation: (a) for the first release** (council 72c; Claude agrees, withdrawing its lean for (b)). It is the only option\n   105\t  that guarantees no number forecast reaches a reader through prose. (b) remains a measured later step.\n   106\t\n   107\t## 5. Tests and the $0 release check (each names its row above)\n   108\t\n   109\t- **Fixtures (real store on a temporary path):**\n   110\t  - a number question with `lo`/`hi`;\n   111\t  - one with bounds only in its conditions;\n   112\t  - an unresolved one with a key;\n   113\t  - a Yes/No question with numeric bounds;\n   114\t  - an event question;\n   115\t  - a Yes/No judgement whose prose quotes a number band;\n   116\t  - a real closing switch;\n   117\t  - an idea.\n   118\t- **What the tests assert.** `release_export`'s output holds only allow-listed keys (a schema check that fails on any extra key). For\n   119\t  number questions it holds no band, ladder, reasons, history, date or closing band; Yes/No follows §4's choice. The static build\n   120\t  refuses foreign input, and a release page makes no network fetch.\n   121\t- **Mutants:**\n   122\t  - an extra field;\n   123\t  - a fetch left on;\n   124\t  - a ladder read in idea composition;\n   125\t  - the identity mis-sorting each fixture.\n   126\t\n   127\t  Each must fail.\n   128\t- **End-to-end acceptance (council 72c):**\n   129\t  - an idea whose only question is `old-1/v8`: the card keeps its sources and \"Forecast unavailable\", with no scored driver and no\n   130\t    substitute band (the current composite expects an endpoint for every scoring candidate, `idea_composite.py:214`, `:231`);\n   131\t  - in the same release package, the two known event answers keep their labels and carry no spending forecast under the chosen\n   132\t    prose rule.\n   133\t- **The $0 release check.**\n   134\t  - On `old-1/v8`, confirm the marker and the same sources in the page and in the export data.\n   135\t  - Exercise closure on a temporary copy with a real closing switch, after first confirming that the unrestricted response exposes the\n   136\t    final band there.\n   137\t  - Check ideas with a recorded or test transport, inspecting the composed request.\n   138\t  - Use `old-3/v36` and `old-1/v10` as the Yes/No prose cases.\n   139\t  - Use one unchanged event question as the control.\n   140\t\n   141\t## 6. Not in scope\n   142\t\n   143\t- The judging, opening and extraction pieces (frozen).\n   144\t- The closed v13s line.\n   145\t- Other open defects.\n   146\t- No prompt or pipeline change.\n   147\t- The POC's own behaviour.\n 11830\t- **Alex's answer** (2026-11-23): \"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线 (推荐)\".\n 11831\t- **Decided (Alex):**\n 11832\t  - The v13s judge line ends at its STOP. Nothing from it enters the product, and poc-v118 stays the product (D690).\n 11833\t  - The first release carries D726: number questions show the question and its sources with \"Forecast unavailable\", the band, the\n 11834\t    forecast text and the history withheld together.\n 11835\t  - The one next step, when release work opens, is a $0 check of the reader's screen on a stored number question that has a\n 11836\t    forecast and history: only the question, its sources and \"Forecast unavailable\" appear.\n 11837\t- **Kept for the record, not built:**\n 11838\t  - the D725 consistency finding (separate answers contradicted each other in 8 of 9 pairs, joint answers in none);\n 11839\t  - the open checker defects in `PAID-V13S-RESULT.md` §5;\n 11840\t  - the v13s request and harness in `docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/`.\n 11841\t\n 11842\t## D757 · 2026-11-23 · Toward production: the \"Forecast unavailable\" release design is ready for when Alex opens release work (council 72–72d); two choices go to Alex\n 11843\t\n 11844\t- **Why.** Alex's direction tonight was to converge and head toward production (D750), and he chose to release with \"Forecast\n 11845\t  unavailable\" (D756). D726 says it \"is built with the release work, which is not started\". Council 72 agreed that opening release\n 11846\t  work is Alex's call, so tonight's step is the design, not the build.\n 11847\t- **The gap, measured at $0** (`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md` §1):\n 11848\t  - today every reader of a number question can see its forecast: the service, the idea input, the closing text;\n 11849\t  - Yes/No and event explanations can quote number forecasts (`old-3/v36` judgement 799, `old-1/v10` judgement 865).\n 11850\t- **The design, after four review rounds** (`codex-r72.md` … `codex-r72d.md`):\n 11851\t  - one release exporter with an explicit allow-list, called directly by the release builder; the finished package is checked;\n 11852\t  - for a number question, the allow-list holds only the question, its sources and \"Forecast unavailable\";\n 11853\t  - the release reads nothing else: no live POC service, no translated or prepared JSON, no composite trials;\n 11854\t  - identity is structural: a question is a number question unless it is an event measure or a canonical Yes/No pair, and unresolved\n 11855\t    records are withheld and listed. Verified on four stores with no wrong result;\n 11856\t  - tests, mutants and an end-to-end acceptance on `old-1/v8` and the two known event leaks.\n 11857\t  - **Why an allow-list.** Rounds 72 and 72b each found new leak paths in a reader-by-reader design, so revision 3 replaced that\n 11858\t    approach with one structural rule.\n 11859\t- **Open for Alex:**\n 11860\t  1. whether to open release work now (then: build to this design, then the $0 release check);\n 11861\t  2. what questions that are not number questions show in the release:\n 11862\t     - (a) answer and label without explanation text, recommended by the council and Claude;\n 11863\t     - (b) explanations only where the judge was shown no number question's state: 21 of 85 questions at the latest answer, and it\n 11864\t       cannot guarantee that no number forecast is quoted.\n 11865\t- **Not done.** Nothing is built and nothing is committed. The POC is unchanged.\n 11866\t\n 11867\t## D758 · 2026-11-23 · Under D439 the council opens local release work for \"Forecast unavailable\"; non-number questions show no explanation text (§4 a); the v13s checker defects are closed as won't-fix (council 73)\n 11868\t\n 11869\t- **Why the council decides.** Alex is asleep and delegated tonight's decisions (D750: \"这边的决策交给你，还有 Council … 准备要往\n 11870\t  Production 方向去走了\"). He had already chosen the behaviour (D726 \"同意\"; D756 \"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线\"). D757 left two\n 11871\t  choices for him; under D439 a choice that would go to Alex goes to the council when it is reversible and within the limits.\n 11872\t- **Council round 73** (`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/round73-brief.md`, `codex-r73.md`, `claude-r73.md`), consensus:\n 11873\t  1. **Release work opens tonight, local and at $0:** the exporter, the release builder, the package check, tests and mutants, the $0\n 11874\t     release check. Nothing committed, pushed, published or deployed; the POC and colleagues' page unchanged. Reversible: the package\n 11875\t     can be deleted without touching what the POC serves. D726's \"not started\" described the state on 2026-11-22 and set no gate.\n 11876\t  2. **§4 (a):** an event or Yes/No question shows its question, evidence and answer with its original label, and no generated\n 11877\t     explanation. It alone guarantees no number forecast reaches a reader through prose (option (b) cannot: a request carries the\n 11878\t     question's earlier reasoning, `views/judging.py:211`). The cost is real: readers lose the written rationale for those answers.\n 11879\t  3. **The v13s checker defects** (`PAID-V13S-RESULT.md` §5) are closed as won't-fix: `calc_small.py` has callers only in research\n 11880\t     code, the line is closed (D756), and the STOP bars tuning on the 36 answers. The findings stay on record.\n 11881\t  4. **Order:** the exporter and the checked package first; the reader's screen second (it completes D756's screen check). How the\n 11882\t     idea path enters the release is settled in the build design's review (round 74).\n 11883\t- **Still Alex's:** commit, push, publish, deploy, colleagues' POC page, any paid send or judge work.\n 11884\t\n 11885\t## D759 · 2026-11-23 · Slice 1 of the \"Forecast unavailable\" release is built and accepted at $0 (councils 74–74j design, 75–75g build); nothing committed or published\n 11886\t\n 11887\t- **Under D439 and D758.** Release work was opened by council 73 (D758). This slice carries it out locally at $0. Nothing is\n 11888\t  committed, pushed, published or deployed. The POC is unchanged: no POC code imports the release module.\n 11889\t- **The design** (`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-BUILD.md`):\n 11890\t  - revision 10 was ready per council 74j, after ten rounds (74 to 74j);\n 11891\t  - revision 11 records the build changes required by councils 75 to 75f.\n 11892\t\n 11893\t  It holds:\n 11894\t  - one allow-listed exporter: a number question carries its question, its evidence in force and \"Forecast unavailable\"; an event or\n 11895\t    Yes/No question carries its question, evidence and answer labels (D758 §4 a);\n 11896\t  - the writer refuses an off-list field;\n 11897\t  - the pass condition: every package field compared with its stored source at the bound, derived from the store;\n 11898\t  - a staged check before one atomic no-replace publication (`renamex_np` with `RENAME_EXCL`);\n 11899\t  - reports published by a no-replace link;\n 11900\t  - canonical days; keys counted only once visible at the bound; store paths free of URI syntax; package files read once.\n 11901\t- **Built:** `src/hivemind/release.py`, `scripts/release_build.py`, `tests/test_release.py`.\n 11902\t- **Proof** (`RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md`):\n 11903\t  - 36 release tests;\n 11904\t  - full suite 425 passed;\n 11905\t  - 31 of 32 mutants caught by failing tests. The 32nd, the canonical-day check, is equivalent on Python 3.10; under 3.13 it is shown\n 11906\t    to stop a package dated 2026-08-25 from carrying evidence through 2026-09-20;\n 11907\t  - the $0 release check on `old-1`, `old-2`, `old-3` and the served ledger (`poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23g/`), passing every\n 11908\t    item it names:\n 11909\t    - every field matches its store (69,636 to 91,055 fields per store);\n 11910\t    - Morningstar's $361 billion, the \"Bullish confirmation\" quote and the analysts' $390 billion are kept;\n 11911\t    - the system's own \"About $390 billion\" forecast, substituted into a summary or added to the manifest, is refused with its exact\n 11912\t      reason;\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
