{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"agent_message","text":"**Not ready to build.** A `v8` card could show both “Forecast unavailable” and “Forecast: $361 billion” and pass the proposed screen check. The $361 billion is a genuine Morningstar estimate. Showing it separately as Hivemind’s forecast would change what the reader sees while leaving every checked field correct. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:174](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:174) · [RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md:124](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md:124)\n\n| Round-76 finding | Revision-2 assessment |\n|---|---|\n| 1. Source links | **Closed.** Addresses render as plain text. The expanded-page check requires zero links, `href` attributes, or `src` attributes. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:82](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:82) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:179](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:179) |\n| 2. Embedded JSON | **Closed.** The literal escapes and header order are explicit. The browser must show the fixture’s exact quote after expansion and find zero image elements. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:48](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:48) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:189](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:189) |\n| 3. Format 2 and package checks | **Closed in design.** The checker hashes and compares the same page bytes, and a wrong page hash alone must fail. The instruction to regenerate the page for altered test data applies to both existing helpers, including the one in the test suite. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:114](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:114) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:130](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:130) · [test_release.py:180](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:180) |\n| 4. What the cards actually show | **Still open.** Revision 2 pins all 1,284 `v8` entries, preserves genuine uses of “Bullish,” and checks reopening. Two gaps remain below. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:165](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:165) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:173](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:173) |\n| 5. Blocked fetch | **Closed.** Observation starts before navigation. The altered script must render the normal list, and Chrome must name both the intended address and `connect-src` in its security error. I found no further request path in the specified page. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:158](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:158) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:192](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:192) |\n| 6. Browser acceptance conditions | **Partly closed.** The fallback, navigation start time, and 390-pixel width check are concrete. The timer still stops when the list exists in the DOM, which can precede visibility. The dark-background check also lacks a fixed expected colour. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:40](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:40) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:205](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:205) · [tokens.css:3](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/web/design-system/tokens.css:3) |\n\n**Two corrections are needed before build.**\n\n1. **Check the whole visible card.** Reading named elements and searching the remaining text for five labels, five conditions, and one forecast prefix lets the extra “Forecast: $361 billion” line pass. Compare the complete visible `v8` card with its expected contents, collapsed and expanded, preserving the grouping of each quote with its sources. A decisive test is to add that one visible line while leaving every named element intact. Use the same visibility requirement for the timer’s end point so a hidden list cannot meet the three-second budget. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:176](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:176) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:180](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:180) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:210](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:210)\n2. **Take each dated card’s expected contents from its own accepted package.** Line 166 names only the default September 20 `old-1` package. I checked the stored files. Its `v36` asks about MediaTek financing. The August 25 `old-3/v36` asks whether NVIDIA will begin shipping Rubin Ultra. Each dated card has exactly one evidence entry, yet both proposed checks could pass with an empty expanded panel because they ask only whether forbidden phrases are absent. Freeze each day, question, answer, and single evidence entry from its dated package, then require that entry and its source to be visible. The existing acceptance script identifies both package paths. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:165](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:165) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:184](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:184) · [release_check.py:208](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:208)\n\n**Optional.** Choose the literal dark background before the first run. The referenced stylesheet defines `--ink` as `#0f140d` and declares a light colour scheme. If `--ink` is the intended dark background, the browser check can expect `rgb(15, 20, 13)` directly. [tokens.css:8](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/web/design-system/tokens.css:8) · [tokens.css:21](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/web/design-system/tokens.css:21)\n\nThis was a read-only design review against the stored packages. Slice 2 has no implementation yet, so browser behavior remains to be verified during the build. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:3](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:3)"}}
